  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 5% cap with numeric per-model results given to purchasers but not the public, and lets existing models stay on sale for 36 months with no numeric interim cap, which benefits Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 makes an 8-per-100k annual incident rate an automatic mandatory recall with no transition, which hits Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) and does not touch Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4). S1 is limited to serious events (24-hour reporting, 2-day customer notice) with no deadline for minor thermal incidents, which is weakened relative to the answer key."
